WEBVTT

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.614
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.697 --> 00:32.241
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.324 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:38.705 --> 00:42.793
Last year's blue crab festival logo
put too much emphasis on the crab,

00:42.876 --> 00:44.711
making it look
like a fish market promotion.

00:44.795 --> 00:46.838
I think that was a bit unfortunate.

00:47.214 --> 00:48.966
So, Merry Design Studio

00:50.133 --> 00:53.595
came up with a design
that portrays a festival

00:53.679 --> 00:56.181
you can enjoy
with family, friends, and dates.

00:57.015 --> 01:01.144
Also, the souvenirs you'll give out
to the visitors

01:01.228 --> 01:06.358
will include the cute crab image
that we designed.

01:07.234 --> 01:08.443
Like this.

01:09.152 --> 01:10.946
GENERAL EVALUATION:
I DO NOT WISH TO SELECT THIS COMPANY

01:13.699 --> 01:16.785
Ms. Yoo, do you like blue crabs?

01:17.035 --> 01:18.245
Of course, I do.

01:18.453 --> 01:20.831
I'm a blue crab killer.

01:20.914 --> 01:23.625
I can eat about three in a sitting.

01:23.709 --> 01:28.672
Ohh! Say there's a big one
and a small one. Which would you prefer?

01:28.755 --> 01:31.967
Of course, I prefer a big, fleshy one.

01:32.050 --> 01:34.595
The salty, flavorful taste
of a fat crab...

01:34.678 --> 01:37.139
My mouth is watering already.

01:37.222 --> 01:38.890
So, you like them big.

01:39.391 --> 01:41.018
There's more to it than just the size.

01:43.103 --> 01:45.022
Ms. Yoo, you're not married, are you?

01:45.605 --> 01:46.940
- No.
- Hmm.

01:49.192 --> 01:51.153
Show her what's good.

01:51.236 --> 01:53.864
She likes them big and fleshy.

01:54.614 --> 01:56.700
He's known as the Hongju City Killer.

01:56.783 --> 01:58.493
Good luck with him.

01:58.827 --> 02:01.038
- Watch yourself.
- I will.

02:01.580 --> 02:02.622
2025 BLUE CRAB FESTIVAL
DESIGN PITCH

02:02.706 --> 02:04.833
Sir, what you just said.

02:04.916 --> 02:07.127
May I ask exactly what you meant?

02:08.128 --> 02:09.713
Pardon? What did I say?

02:09.796 --> 02:11.965
You wished me good luck.

02:12.049 --> 02:13.967
Good luck with what, exactly?

02:14.051 --> 02:15.761
Why don't you wrap up your presentation?

02:15.844 --> 02:18.764
We're short on time,
so don't try to pick a fight.

02:18.847 --> 02:20.265
I'm not picking a fight.

02:20.974 --> 02:24.102
I just want to know
what you meant when you said--

02:24.186 --> 02:25.937
- Ms. Yoo?
- Yes?

02:26.021 --> 02:27.022
Don't you want the job?

02:27.773 --> 02:30.275
We wanted to give
an obscure company a project,

02:30.359 --> 02:33.070
but who'd want to work
with someone so aggressive?

02:42.996 --> 02:43.997
Fine.

02:44.081 --> 02:45.123
Don't work with me.

02:46.833 --> 02:48.043
I refuse the job.

02:49.211 --> 02:50.712
I'm sorry, but to be honest,

02:51.171 --> 02:53.924
I'm picky about who I work with myself.

02:54.007 --> 02:56.468
I might as well say this
since I won't get the job.

02:56.551 --> 02:58.136
You there.

03:00.639 --> 03:02.933
Yes, you. The man who just pointed.

03:03.016 --> 03:05.227
Do you think you hold a lot of power?

03:06.603 --> 03:09.773
You might have the advantage here,
but outside, I have the upper hand.

03:09.856 --> 03:12.484
My taxes pay your salary.

03:13.902 --> 03:15.028
I had no idea

03:15.112 --> 03:18.615
my tax money ended up
in the pockets of such trash.

03:18.699 --> 03:20.242
What?

03:20.325 --> 03:22.077
What did you just say?

03:22.160 --> 03:23.704
- Me?
- Yes, you.

03:23.787 --> 03:26.081
- How old are you?
- Why would you ask my age?

03:26.164 --> 03:29.167
- How dare she talk like that?
- Are you jealous that I'm young?

03:29.709 --> 03:31.503
You dare take that tone with me?

03:31.586 --> 03:33.422
- Let go of me.
- Leave it.

03:33.505 --> 03:37.175
- Do you look down on our city?
- No, Hongju City is blameless.

03:37.801 --> 03:40.637
JAMYANG PRINT SHOP

03:45.642 --> 03:48.812
So basically,
you caused a stir and got kicked out.

03:48.895 --> 03:50.105
Don't worry.

03:50.188 --> 03:51.314
You're my only employee.

03:51.398 --> 03:53.024
I'll manage to pay you somehow.

03:53.108 --> 03:54.359
I doubt that.

03:55.444 --> 03:57.612
We scored zero projects this month.

03:57.696 --> 03:59.489
How will you pay this month's rent?

04:00.157 --> 04:02.617
Did we get any inquiries
on our social platforms?

04:03.034 --> 04:06.413
Stay on the line while I go and see.

04:09.708 --> 04:12.377
I think we got a couple of small jobs.

04:13.336 --> 04:14.421
2 PROJECTS UNDERWAY

04:14.504 --> 04:16.631
Giveaways for a new butcher shop

04:16.715 --> 04:18.383
and a logo for a Magok coffee shop.

04:18.467 --> 04:21.928
The coffee shop owner wants to see
a portfolio before they decide.

04:22.012 --> 04:24.306
Should we send our old herbal tea design?

04:24.389 --> 04:26.641
Sure, will you come back to the office?

04:26.725 --> 04:28.059
Oh, no. I have to drop by

04:28.143 --> 04:30.645
a nearby department store
while I'm out in Euljiro.

04:30.729 --> 04:32.939
You can finish the draft and go home.

04:37.277 --> 04:38.403
Sir.

04:40.113 --> 04:43.617
Could you lower
the saturation of this part

04:43.700 --> 04:45.577
while keeping the color Pantone 213?

04:45.660 --> 04:46.661
I lowered it already.

04:46.745 --> 04:50.624
Yes, but the case is transparent,
so it'll look different when it's filled.

04:50.707 --> 04:52.667
You can't mind that, too. Who will notice?

04:52.751 --> 04:54.336
A reprint will just cost you more.

04:54.419 --> 04:55.921
I know the difference.

04:56.004 --> 04:59.257
I can't sell anything to a customer
if something bothers me.

04:59.341 --> 05:00.342
You're too picky.

05:00.634 --> 05:02.052
You'll never make a fortune doing that.

05:03.553 --> 05:04.679
Sir.

05:05.055 --> 05:06.056
Thank you.

05:13.730 --> 05:16.566
We engraved the wedding bands
with your initials.

05:17.317 --> 05:18.318
Thanks.

05:18.401 --> 05:21.530
The receipt, warranty card,
and raffle ticket are inside.

05:21.613 --> 05:23.156
Thank you.

05:23.240 --> 05:24.908
Thank you. Goodbye.

05:28.119 --> 05:31.206
I emailed a copy
of my boyfriend's passport.

05:31.665 --> 05:32.874
Yes, Kim Wooju.

05:33.542 --> 05:35.126
Thank you. Bye.

05:37.212 --> 05:40.549
That's the honeymoon booked.

05:43.051 --> 05:45.011
WHEN WILL YOU BE DONE?

05:52.143 --> 05:53.270
I love you.

06:12.414 --> 06:13.748
When will you be done?

06:15.292 --> 06:16.751
I'm in a meeting.

06:17.043 --> 06:18.670
You're working late again today?

06:18.753 --> 06:19.796
YOU'RE WORKING LATE AGAIN TODAY?

06:19.880 --> 06:20.881
It must be tiresome.

06:20.964 --> 06:21.965
- Who is it?
- You've got this.

06:22.090 --> 06:23.174
-  I love you.
What did she say?

06:32.726 --> 06:35.228
I was hoping to have dinner
with him.

06:35.312 --> 06:36.354
Oh, gosh.

06:36.438 --> 06:37.606
Sorry.

06:41.860 --> 06:43.069
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

06:43.153 --> 06:45.238
EPISODE 1

06:49.284 --> 06:50.660
ALWAYS ACCEPT AN APOLOGY

06:50.744 --> 06:52.579
CUTE WOOJU
NEVER LET A FIGHT LAST MORE THAN A DAY

06:52.662 --> 06:54.039
WOOJU TAKES OUT THE RECYCLING

06:54.122 --> 06:55.624
HANDWRITE LETTERS ON ANNIVERSARIES

06:55.707 --> 06:57.042
TAKE A MONTHLY TRIP IN KOREA

06:57.626 --> 06:59.711
Forget the wedding and whatnot.

06:59.794 --> 07:01.171
I wish I could call it all off.

07:03.256 --> 07:04.591
Oh, Meri.

07:05.675 --> 07:08.970
You can't just register your marriage
and say it's done.

07:09.054 --> 07:11.681
- It's a hassle, but a necessary one.
- Mom.

07:11.765 --> 07:14.351
The problem is that there's so much to do.

07:14.434 --> 07:16.061
I have so little money to spare,

07:16.144 --> 07:18.730
but Wooju's mother
keeps going on about a hotel.

07:18.813 --> 07:20.607
It's driving me up the wall.

07:21.316 --> 07:24.402
If she has the money for a hotel wedding,
she should contribute to our rent.

07:24.486 --> 07:27.947
Her son has a fancy degree,
and her husband's a university professor.

07:28.365 --> 07:30.533
She has an appearance to keep up.

07:30.617 --> 07:32.369
Try to understand.

07:33.036 --> 07:34.079
Where are you?

07:34.162 --> 07:35.538
- Did you have dinner?
- Yes.

07:36.039 --> 07:37.165
I ate.

07:38.041 --> 07:39.876
I'm at our new place.

07:40.627 --> 07:43.713
I come by whenever I can
to unpack and organize stuff.

07:45.173 --> 07:47.842
Did you have dinner, Mom?

07:47.926 --> 07:49.803
I did. What about Wooju?

07:49.886 --> 07:52.305
He moved in already.

07:53.807 --> 07:56.101
He didn't call to tell you?

07:57.185 --> 08:00.230
He must know we couldn't afford this place
without your help.

08:00.313 --> 08:01.898
Leave it.

08:01.981 --> 08:04.484
I gave you the money
so he'd be good to you.

08:04.567 --> 08:08.071
Let me give you a word of caution.

08:08.154 --> 08:10.990
Don't nag him for not having
contributed to the deposit.

08:11.074 --> 08:13.118
You shouldn't discourage a man.

08:13.201 --> 08:15.286
What? Why would he be discouraged?

08:15.370 --> 08:17.122
I cater to him in every way.

08:17.205 --> 08:20.375
I'm good wife material
that's rare these days.

08:20.458 --> 08:21.960
You're the kid out of the two of us.

08:24.421 --> 08:25.505
Mom.

08:26.172 --> 08:28.341
I'll make lots of money

08:28.425 --> 08:30.468
and pay you back soo--

08:31.136 --> 08:32.846
What's the matter?

08:33.555 --> 08:34.681
It's fine.

08:34.764 --> 08:36.683
I just stepped on something.

08:39.352 --> 08:42.981
Mom, I'll call you back a bit later.

08:43.898 --> 08:44.941
Bye.

08:55.076 --> 08:56.453
What is this?

08:57.287 --> 08:58.663
It's not my...

09:36.618 --> 09:38.787
I look like a model.

09:43.124 --> 09:44.334
What about this?

09:44.417 --> 09:46.669
It's when I played golf
with some investors.

09:47.337 --> 09:48.338
I know that.

09:49.005 --> 09:50.590
- A comment on that post.
- Yes.

09:51.925 --> 09:53.093
"Sweet Jenny 97."

09:54.260 --> 09:57.305
- What?
- She liked every single post of yours.

09:57.847 --> 09:59.933
SWEET_JENNY97
YOUR FACE IS ALL I SEE

10:00.725 --> 10:02.477
You follow each other. Who is that?

10:05.021 --> 10:06.773
She's just a colleague of mine.

10:07.398 --> 10:09.400
Didn't I mention her? I bet I did.

10:09.484 --> 10:12.153
She went to school in Hong Kong.

10:12.237 --> 10:13.363
Did you sleep with her?

10:17.575 --> 10:18.993
Hey.

10:19.077 --> 10:20.120
What's up with you?

10:20.203 --> 10:22.872
Why the heck would I sleep with her?

10:27.252 --> 10:29.420
Then why did I find this by the bed?

10:30.046 --> 10:31.131
What's this?

10:49.858 --> 10:53.153
Oh, I was at a company workshop
in Gangwon-do last week.

10:53.486 --> 10:55.405
A few colleagues came by to look around.

10:55.738 --> 10:58.575
- Colleagues?
- You see, they were dead curious.

10:59.075 --> 11:01.327
She must have dropped it then.

11:02.412 --> 11:04.038
I should give it back.

11:05.498 --> 11:09.878
Last week, your department head
went fishing on Anmyeondo Island.

11:11.588 --> 11:14.757
Your section chief
took his kids to Lotte World.

11:15.675 --> 11:16.885
Assistant Manager Jang.

11:17.886 --> 11:20.555
He went to the wedding
of a guy he met in the army.

11:21.681 --> 11:23.433
The Gangwon-do workshop...

11:25.393 --> 11:26.978
Did you and Jenny go on your own?

11:32.692 --> 11:33.818
Sunset Resort.

11:34.903 --> 11:36.696
Each suite has a private pool.

11:36.779 --> 11:40.158
You were there overnight,
so I don't need to ask what went on.

11:40.950 --> 11:42.285
What do you think?

11:42.368 --> 11:43.703
If you keep denying it,

11:44.621 --> 11:47.165
should I cause a scene at your office
like some soap opera?

11:54.923 --> 11:55.924
Hey.

12:01.721 --> 12:02.847
Fine.

12:02.931 --> 12:04.807
I'll come clean.

12:04.891 --> 12:06.434
I'm Adam, who fell for a snake's lies.

12:06.517 --> 12:08.645
I partook of the forbidden fruit. So what?

12:10.647 --> 12:11.981
"So what?"

12:12.732 --> 12:14.234
Why do you think I did?

12:15.193 --> 12:17.362
It was because I was under so much stress.

12:18.112 --> 12:19.948
My investors call every day
about profit margins,

12:20.031 --> 12:21.950
while I'm just a newbie
with a wedding coming up.

12:22.033 --> 12:23.785
Don't you see how much is on my mind?

12:23.868 --> 12:26.663
I was already on edge,
and you nagged me so much.

12:26.746 --> 12:29.290
You called, texted, and bossed me about
with the wedding prep.

12:29.374 --> 12:30.792
I felt like I was being fried.

12:30.875 --> 12:33.002
Am I getting married on my own?

12:33.920 --> 12:35.213
I work full-time, too.

12:35.380 --> 12:37.674
- I'm busy, too!
- I know you are!

12:37.757 --> 12:39.008
That's why I...

12:42.220 --> 12:43.304
I'm sorry.

12:44.472 --> 12:45.765
I'm a jerk.

12:46.933 --> 12:48.017
I deserve a beating!

12:49.185 --> 12:51.062
Say a number. How many slaps?

12:53.106 --> 12:54.774
I know you have a glib tongue.

12:56.276 --> 12:57.443
But not today.

12:59.070 --> 13:00.697
I won't let you off like that today.

13:04.617 --> 13:07.912
Meri. Let's think rationally.

13:08.579 --> 13:10.415
We booked a wedding hall,
got a marriage license,

13:10.498 --> 13:11.541
and rented an apartment.

13:11.624 --> 13:13.668
Leave me, and you'll be a divorcée
even without a wedding.

13:13.751 --> 13:15.461
Wow, isn't that so unfair?

13:15.545 --> 13:16.546
It is unfair!

13:16.629 --> 13:18.381
Right? That makes zero sense.

13:19.340 --> 13:20.675
That girl, Jenny...

13:21.759 --> 13:22.969
She's just a fling.

13:31.227 --> 13:33.479
And you and I will be together forever.

13:34.188 --> 13:35.815
It was a one-time mistake,

13:36.107 --> 13:37.692
and I ended it with her already.

13:46.242 --> 13:47.368
JENNY

13:47.452 --> 13:48.703
When are you coming over?

13:48.786 --> 13:51.164
I'm waiting for you in the underwear
you got me yesterday.

13:51.247 --> 13:52.248
Isn't it pretty?

14:01.340 --> 14:02.592
It's my section chief.

14:02.675 --> 14:04.010
About tomorrow's business trip.

14:05.261 --> 14:07.680
Did I ever ask to see your phone?

14:09.515 --> 14:10.600
No.

14:11.350 --> 14:12.477
I have a bad feeling.

14:13.227 --> 14:16.189
If I don't see this now,
I might doubt you forever and ever.

14:16.689 --> 14:17.690
Move your hand.

14:28.367 --> 14:29.577
What are you doing?

14:29.660 --> 14:31.120
It was my section chief.

14:31.204 --> 14:32.455
Let me see it.

14:32.538 --> 14:33.539
It was my section chief, okay?

14:33.623 --> 14:35.166
Exactly, that's why I want to see.

14:35.249 --> 14:36.334
Why see my section chief's...

14:42.215 --> 14:43.299
Are you all right?

14:43.382 --> 14:44.550
- Did he step on her hand?
- Hey.

14:44.634 --> 14:45.635
He stomped on her hand.

14:45.718 --> 14:47.428
- What's going on?
- Is she okay?

14:49.180 --> 14:51.474
Why did you try to see my phone?

14:52.183 --> 14:54.602
You shouldn't cross the line
however close you are with someone.

14:56.687 --> 14:57.772
Let's see your hand.

15:00.817 --> 15:01.818
"The line?"

15:03.778 --> 15:05.571
You're the one who crossed the line.

15:06.697 --> 15:08.783
That apartment is ours,
and we're soon to be married.

15:09.325 --> 15:11.244
You brought another woman over.

15:12.745 --> 15:14.330
- No way.
- How could you do that?

15:14.997 --> 15:16.457
Is he out of his mind?

15:21.003 --> 15:23.881
For seven months
after you got your new job,

15:24.799 --> 15:27.093
you always worked late
or had a team dinner.

15:27.510 --> 15:29.345
You were so hard to reach.

15:31.472 --> 15:34.225
You even forgot my birthday
and our anniversary.

15:35.476 --> 15:38.104
I got fitted for a wedding dress on my own
because you were too busy.

15:40.690 --> 15:41.691
I couldn't bear...

15:44.735 --> 15:47.321
the thought of letting
our five years go to waste.

15:49.031 --> 15:52.410
So, I told myself to ignore everything
and just marry you.

15:54.120 --> 15:55.246
But I won't.

15:56.706 --> 15:59.417
I think I'll divorce you one day
even if we do get married.

16:01.544 --> 16:02.962
If it's bound to happen one day,

16:04.463 --> 16:05.756
that might as well be today.

16:08.718 --> 16:09.719
Meri.

16:21.439 --> 16:23.065
She actually drenched him.

16:23.316 --> 16:25.526
- Did you see that?
- That was insane.

16:31.908 --> 16:35.703
She's pretty old, you see,
and I need to sit next to her.

16:35.786 --> 16:37.997
- Is it for health concerns?
- Yes.

16:38.080 --> 16:39.916
Could you get him to swap with me?

16:39.999 --> 16:42.168
I'll ask the gentleman
for you.

16:42.251 --> 16:43.961
- Will you come with me?
- Sure.

16:44.462 --> 16:46.172
- Let's go.
- Yes, thanks.

16:50.134 --> 16:51.427
Sir?

16:51.510 --> 16:53.429
Were you assigned seat 5D?

16:54.096 --> 16:55.139
Yes.

16:55.223 --> 16:56.682
This gentleman says

16:56.766 --> 17:00.228
he was given a seat
apart from his elderly mother.

17:00.311 --> 17:02.230
He'd like to know
if you could switch with him.

17:02.730 --> 17:04.190
I'm so sorry.

17:04.273 --> 17:06.067
My mother is very old,

17:06.150 --> 17:09.028
and I need to assist her
during the flight.

17:09.987 --> 17:11.530
Will you swap with me, sir?

17:12.114 --> 17:13.199
I don't want to.

17:13.950 --> 17:16.410
My seat is also in business class.

17:18.579 --> 17:19.914
Sir?

17:22.458 --> 17:23.459
Hello?

17:31.801 --> 17:34.637
We have reached our destination

17:34.804 --> 17:36.931
at Incheon International Airport.

17:37.723 --> 17:40.309
When opening overhead storage
after the plane stops,

17:40.393 --> 17:42.937
please take care to ensure
nothing falls out.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.021
Thank you.

17:47.692 --> 17:50.611
14 HOURS PRIOR

17:51.529 --> 17:54.323
The old hag's trying to run away
without selling the land,

17:54.782 --> 17:57.827
so I'll sit next to her
and get her to sign the papers.

17:59.161 --> 18:01.998
My big sister in Seoul
won't let me anywhere near Mom.

18:02.081 --> 18:05.585
I need to get the papers signed
on the plane.

18:05.668 --> 18:07.420
Mom could die any day now.

18:07.503 --> 18:09.714
That's why I need the papers signed soon.

18:11.549 --> 18:12.633
Ma'am.

18:13.509 --> 18:16.262
Keep the land deeds until the day you die.

18:16.345 --> 18:18.389
Don't trust your son
and hand it right over.

18:18.472 --> 18:20.474
You can't trust anyone out there.

18:34.822 --> 18:36.115
I just landed.

18:36.198 --> 18:37.283
I'm going straight to Yangyang.

18:38.409 --> 18:39.410
You rotten fool.

18:39.869 --> 18:41.495
Why not drop by to say hi first?

18:42.288 --> 18:44.540
I made a video call
before I got on the plane.

18:44.624 --> 18:46.500
It's not that I want to see you.

18:47.001 --> 18:48.336
I picked too many zucchinis.

18:48.419 --> 18:49.795
I can't eat it all.

18:49.879 --> 18:53.883
Put them in the freezer.
I'll eat them when I'm back.

18:53.966 --> 18:56.469
You never say you'll come by.

18:56.552 --> 18:59.972
I'm scared you'll put me right to work.

19:00.056 --> 19:02.433
Grandma, it's my first holiday
in three years.

19:03.392 --> 19:04.810
I'll let you off just this once.

19:04.894 --> 19:06.520
Just wait until you start work.

19:06.604 --> 19:09.649
How can you only think about putting
your one and only grandson to work?

19:09.732 --> 19:11.984
I spent a fortune to feed and educate you.

19:12.068 --> 19:14.362
I have a long way to go
to make up for the tuition I invested.

19:14.445 --> 19:16.155
You're so calculative.

19:16.238 --> 19:18.491
A peddler's not a peddler
if they're not calculative.

19:18.574 --> 19:19.784
Okay, fine.

19:20.409 --> 19:23.496
Good luck with the zucchinis
and sweet potatoes while I'm away.

19:23.579 --> 19:24.622
See you in a month.

19:26.707 --> 19:27.750
I'll be in touch.

19:38.969 --> 19:40.846
You prepared a lot of food.

19:40.930 --> 19:43.849
- Shall I stay and eat with you?
- No.

19:44.642 --> 19:47.978
He survived on hamburgers
in a foreign country without his parents.

19:48.062 --> 19:50.439
I was hoping to feed him
some home-cooked food.

21:32.291 --> 21:33.709
HAPPINESS

21:54.730 --> 21:56.899
ONE MONTH LATER

21:56.982 --> 21:58.692
The one-month consideration period
has ended,

21:59.360 --> 22:04.073
and I confirm Kim Wooju
and Yoo Meri's intent to divorce.

22:10.246 --> 22:12.581
I can't believe
all the things you make me do.

22:13.082 --> 22:14.875
Stupid me.

22:14.959 --> 22:17.545
I shouldn't have registered our marriage
when you asked to.

22:17.628 --> 22:19.880
It was the only way to get your mother
to pay the housing deposit.

22:19.964 --> 22:21.674
Are you saying
she forced you against your will?

22:21.799 --> 22:23.217
- You--
- That's not true.

22:29.014 --> 22:31.559
- What did your mother say?
- She didn't say anything.

22:32.101 --> 22:35.145
I couldn't tell her I became a divorcée
before I even walked down the aisle.

22:36.105 --> 22:37.356
Sorry.

22:38.524 --> 22:40.025
I'll tell her later when the time's right.

22:40.568 --> 22:42.778
I said we'd postpone the wedding
because you're busy.

22:42.862 --> 22:44.154
Keep that in mind.

22:45.281 --> 22:46.282
Okay.

22:47.700 --> 22:49.952
I'll vacate the apartment,
so take your stuff.

22:50.953 --> 22:52.162
Are you moving out?

22:52.246 --> 22:53.873
Do you want me to live there when you...

22:53.956 --> 22:55.708
I took out a massive loan.

22:56.458 --> 22:57.459
You're right.

22:59.545 --> 23:01.130
You'll have much less debt, at least.

23:01.297 --> 23:02.715
It's a good thing we broke up.

23:03.173 --> 23:04.925
Sure, it's just great.

23:05.009 --> 23:06.802
I'm so grateful I could cry.

23:06.886 --> 23:08.095
I have much less debt.

23:17.563 --> 23:18.564
Hi, Jenny.

23:20.274 --> 23:21.525
Are you at the airport already?

23:22.109 --> 23:23.652
Yes, I'm just about to leave.

23:24.361 --> 23:25.362
Okay, see you soon.

23:30.951 --> 23:32.870
I'm going somewhere on holiday.

23:33.871 --> 23:35.497
I have to hand in our divorce decree.

23:35.581 --> 23:36.582
Did you fill in your details?

23:37.917 --> 23:39.126
Yes.

23:39.209 --> 23:40.544
Thanks for submitting it for me.

23:41.003 --> 23:42.254
Don't thank me.

23:42.338 --> 23:43.589
I'm doing it in case you don't.

23:46.008 --> 23:48.344
Hey, don't hate me too much.

23:49.178 --> 23:50.179
We were

23:51.722 --> 23:53.182
in love for a while.

23:59.438 --> 24:00.439
Meri.

24:00.773 --> 24:01.857
Live a good life.

24:01.941 --> 24:02.983
Forget all about me.

24:06.278 --> 24:07.321
Wooju.

24:08.155 --> 24:09.156
Get lost.

24:11.408 --> 24:13.744
Hey, you should find a good guy.

24:13.827 --> 24:15.454
Don't wait too long.

24:15.537 --> 24:18.207
You get over love with love!

24:23.420 --> 24:24.755
I'm on my way now.

24:28.842 --> 24:30.177
Darn you!

24:39.645 --> 24:43.524
HOME APPLIANCE FAIR FOR NEWLYWEDS

24:43.607 --> 24:45.484
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

24:55.995 --> 24:57.579
RIZZ WEDDING HALL

24:57.663 --> 25:01.375
THE BLUEMON HALL RESERVATION WAS CANCELED

25:02.543 --> 25:05.462
DREAM TRAVEL AGENTS

25:05.546 --> 25:08.632
YOUR HONEYMOON PACKAGE WAS CANCELED

25:10.676 --> 25:14.054
ELLE WEDDING DRESSES
YOUR WEDDING DRESS RENTAL WAS CANCELED

25:40.205 --> 25:42.583
Do clean breakups exist?

25:57.097 --> 25:59.099
You pretend to be okay.

26:00.434 --> 26:02.227
What's broken

26:03.395 --> 26:05.397
can't be glued back together.

26:25.751 --> 26:27.377
- Meri.
- Yes?

26:28.337 --> 26:30.214
- I love you.
- I love you, too.

26:44.895 --> 26:46.814
I'll live well without you now.

26:55.447 --> 26:57.241
I'll make lots of money.

27:00.410 --> 27:02.913
I'll go on lots of trips.

27:05.124 --> 27:06.875
I'll even go on blind dates.

27:10.838 --> 27:12.506
I'll forget the likes of you...

27:17.886 --> 27:19.012
I'll live...

27:23.267 --> 27:24.434
I'll...

27:27.187 --> 27:28.397
I'll be really busy.

28:01.680 --> 28:02.890
Young man.

28:04.141 --> 28:05.559
I'd grown to like you.

28:05.642 --> 28:06.810
I'm sad to see you go.

28:07.853 --> 28:10.063
They say those who meet must part.

28:10.147 --> 28:11.148
Here.

28:11.356 --> 28:13.358
- Eat it on the way.
- What's this?

28:14.860 --> 28:16.069
Ooh!

28:16.153 --> 28:17.154
It's corn bread.

28:17.237 --> 28:19.197
I got it from the best place nearby.

28:19.781 --> 28:20.866
Just for you.

28:21.909 --> 28:22.910
How is it?

28:23.410 --> 28:25.370
It's good.

28:25.954 --> 28:28.081
I should bring you some bread next time.

28:28.373 --> 28:29.374
Bread?

28:29.458 --> 28:33.295
My family owns the best bakery
in the whole country.

28:33.378 --> 28:34.421
A bakery?

28:34.504 --> 28:36.340
- Hmm.
- Oh!

28:36.423 --> 28:37.466
Thanks for this.

28:37.549 --> 28:39.718
MYUNGSOONDANG

28:40.552 --> 28:41.762
Congratulations.

28:41.845 --> 28:46.642
Myungsoondang won the President's Award
at the Industrial Day award ceremony.

28:46.725 --> 28:48.518
How do you feel?

28:49.436 --> 28:51.021
I don't have much to say,

28:51.104 --> 28:53.273
but that I'm grateful and thankful.

28:53.982 --> 28:55.776
I appreciate the acknowledgement
that I make everything

28:55.859 --> 28:58.820
as if it were for my own child,
using no preservatives.

28:58.904 --> 29:00.572
I can only thank you.

29:00.656 --> 29:02.240
How humble of you.

29:02.324 --> 29:05.035
Myungsoondang is Korea's first-ever bakery

29:05.118 --> 29:06.203
- as well as...
- Your grandma

29:06.286 --> 29:09.790
dumps a whole load of additives
when she cooks.

29:10.207 --> 29:12.334
Just not in the bread.

29:12.417 --> 29:14.962
You should, too,
since your food is horrible.

29:15.045 --> 29:17.214
...you even announced
a new beginning.

29:17.297 --> 29:19.174
- Eat all you want.
- How is that going?

29:19.257 --> 29:22.636
At the Paris Dessert Fair last year,

29:22.719 --> 29:24.972
our hangwa was incredibly popular.

29:25.681 --> 29:27.891
I got many inquiries
from department stores

29:27.975 --> 29:30.060
in Paris, London, and New York,

29:30.143 --> 29:33.313
so I plan to promote
our traditional hangwa

29:33.397 --> 29:35.774
as a K-dessert throughout the world.

29:35.857 --> 29:36.942
KOREA ECONOMY

29:40.070 --> 29:43.198
Chairwoman, can you pose
with one of your products this time?

29:43.281 --> 29:44.366
Yes, sure.

29:45.534 --> 29:46.576
Here you go, Chairwoman.

29:46.660 --> 29:47.995
Get me one of our new products.

29:48.078 --> 29:49.079
Here it is.

29:53.250 --> 29:56.628
Will you take the photo
so the hangwa looks nicer than me?

29:56.712 --> 29:59.214
Mom, you're not shooting a commercial.

29:59.881 --> 30:02.426
Why not make an interview
work as well as one?

30:02.509 --> 30:04.386
Yes, let's milk it for all it's worth.

30:05.303 --> 30:06.513
"Make it worthwhile."

30:06.596 --> 30:07.681
Use nice language.

30:07.764 --> 30:09.057
I used easy language, Mom.

30:11.935 --> 30:13.645
One, two, three.

30:14.229 --> 30:15.814
CHAIRWOMAN KO
WINS ANNUAL PRESIDENT'S AWARD

30:21.653 --> 30:23.405
What did the coffee shop owner say?

30:25.073 --> 30:26.074
Really?

30:26.450 --> 30:27.909
We'll go with a cat, then.

30:27.993 --> 30:28.994
The customer is king.

30:30.203 --> 30:32.372
Let's put just the shop name
on the napkins

30:32.456 --> 30:34.916
and put stickers
on the paper cups and sleeves.

30:35.917 --> 30:37.419
Are the samples at the office?

30:39.129 --> 30:41.214
Oh, yes. I brought them home.

30:43.425 --> 30:45.427
The samples...

30:49.598 --> 30:50.599
Where did I put them?

30:53.393 --> 30:54.478
Here they are.

30:59.649 --> 31:01.068
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

31:02.527 --> 31:04.196
I have to hand in our divorce decree.

31:04.279 --> 31:05.489
Did you fill in your details?

31:06.073 --> 31:07.616
I need to hand this in soon.

31:12.746 --> 31:13.955
Is anyone home?

31:16.291 --> 31:17.626
Is someone in?

31:18.919 --> 31:19.920
POLICE

31:20.003 --> 31:21.922
Do you live here?

31:22.005 --> 31:23.381
Yes, is something wrong?

31:26.218 --> 31:27.636
We meet at last.

31:27.719 --> 31:29.179
JUNGMUN POLICE, SERVING WITH WARMTH

31:29.262 --> 31:30.722
A rental con?

31:31.181 --> 31:33.350
The homeowner had left a realtor

31:33.433 --> 31:35.685
in charge of the property
while she was abroad.

31:35.769 --> 31:37.187
Without the realtor knowing,

31:37.270 --> 31:39.356
their assistant got someone
to pretend to be the homeowner

31:39.439 --> 31:40.899
and sign a fake lease with you.

31:40.982 --> 31:43.568
What happens to me, then?

31:43.652 --> 31:45.237
You have to move out,

31:45.320 --> 31:47.739
or the homeowner
will report you for trespassing.

31:47.823 --> 31:51.076
I can't move out
until I get my security deposit back.

31:51.910 --> 31:55.455
You need to sue the people
who conned you to get that back.

31:58.041 --> 32:01.628
But the fake homeowner is a vagrant
who let the scammer use his identity.

32:02.212 --> 32:04.714
Are you saying
I might not get my money back?

32:11.638 --> 32:12.764
WOOJU

32:17.394 --> 32:19.312
What? A rental con?

32:21.857 --> 32:23.692
You should've looked into it better.

32:24.401 --> 32:26.111
Do you have rental insurance?

32:26.987 --> 32:29.364
Why didn't you do something that basic?

32:30.991 --> 32:32.075
My uncle?

32:33.076 --> 32:34.411
Yes, he's at the Public Prosecutors'...

32:36.037 --> 32:38.415
I can't ask a favor
for something like that.

32:38.999 --> 32:42.669
Don't talk as if it has
nothing to do with you.

32:43.545 --> 32:46.923
I don't know anyone else to ask for help.

32:47.007 --> 32:48.633
Is there nothing you can do?

32:49.509 --> 32:52.721
My savings, a bank loan,
and my mom's money went into it.

32:52.804 --> 32:55.390
It's 300 million won.

32:56.016 --> 32:57.017
Meri.

32:57.559 --> 32:58.894
It does have nothing to do with me.

32:58.977 --> 33:00.395
It's none of my business now.

33:00.478 --> 33:01.938
We're complete strangers now.

33:02.647 --> 33:04.691
You need to accept reality.

33:04.774 --> 33:06.818
Will you call me
whenever something goes wrong?

33:07.777 --> 33:11.072
It's really rude to call your ex
out of the blue like this.

33:11.656 --> 33:15.869
I picked up this time for old time's sake,
but I won't anymore, okay?

33:15.952 --> 33:16.953
No, wait.

33:17.913 --> 33:19.247
Wooju, hello?

33:20.207 --> 33:21.583
WOOJU

33:25.045 --> 33:28.215
The phone is off.
Transferring to voicemail.

33:28.298 --> 33:29.633
Oh, no.

33:31.718 --> 33:34.095
What do I do?

33:39.768 --> 33:41.061
He's right.

33:44.940 --> 33:46.900
We are complete strangers now.

33:48.777 --> 33:49.861
But even so.

33:50.403 --> 33:52.405
We only just broke up.

33:53.365 --> 33:55.033
Is that all he could say?

33:56.952 --> 33:59.663
I haven't even submitted
our divorce decree.

34:13.385 --> 34:14.386
If not for you,

34:15.553 --> 34:18.390
I wouldn't even have
rented that apartment.

34:18.473 --> 34:20.850
And now you're turning your back on me?

34:21.685 --> 34:23.395
What am I to do now?

34:32.320 --> 34:33.571
MOM

34:42.080 --> 34:43.748
Hi, Mom.

34:43.832 --> 34:45.709
Hey, Meri.

34:45.792 --> 34:48.586
I braised some yellow croaker
and seasoned some cucumbers.

34:48.670 --> 34:50.005
Wooju's parents haven't moved, right?

34:50.088 --> 34:51.089
What?

34:52.340 --> 34:54.676
You don't have to send them food.

34:55.176 --> 34:58.013
Let's keep the good food to ourselves.

34:58.096 --> 35:00.849
Why cook for them?
It's extra work for you.

35:00.932 --> 35:04.019
I made a little extra while I was at it.

35:04.102 --> 35:06.771
Cooking a bit more food
doesn't wear my hands or feet.

35:06.855 --> 35:09.065
Just don't send them anything.

35:10.025 --> 35:12.402
Why would you keep sending them stuff?

35:12.485 --> 35:13.570
MERI

35:15.113 --> 35:16.197
What's up with you?

35:16.281 --> 35:18.408
Do they not like my food?

35:19.242 --> 35:22.329
No, it's not that.

35:22.412 --> 35:24.873
There's nothing else I can do for them.

35:24.956 --> 35:27.375
I want to do what I can for you and them.

35:28.543 --> 35:30.962
I can only do this while I'm still able.

35:31.046 --> 35:32.213
I don't have much longer.

35:33.214 --> 35:37.093
My shoulders are beginning
to ache, you know.

35:37.260 --> 35:38.678
Mom.

35:41.848 --> 35:43.099
I'm sorry.

35:43.183 --> 35:44.351
What the heck?

35:44.893 --> 35:49.105
Have you finally grown up
now that it's time to get married?

35:51.274 --> 35:52.275
Meri.

35:52.776 --> 35:56.029
Don't think too much and go to bed.

35:57.072 --> 35:59.532
I have to watch my favorite show. Bye.

36:00.408 --> 36:01.409
Okay, bye.

36:17.676 --> 36:19.177
CHEONGHUN 1-GA

36:19.260 --> 36:20.929
You went off course.

36:21.012 --> 36:23.056
- What?
- Rerouting.

36:24.057 --> 36:25.433
Oh, geez.

36:25.934 --> 36:28.812
Turn right at the next corner.

36:43.034 --> 36:44.619
WOOJU

36:46.871 --> 36:48.665
Kim Wooju, you punk.

36:53.795 --> 36:57.048
Why did it send me this way?

37:03.722 --> 37:04.723
My goodness...

37:04.806 --> 37:07.684
Go straight for 150 meters and turn right.

37:18.945 --> 37:19.946
What was that?

37:27.036 --> 37:28.246
Are you all right?

37:34.627 --> 37:36.254
I'm fine.

37:37.797 --> 37:39.007
Are you really fine?

37:39.090 --> 37:41.843
I'm fine. It hurts a bit, but I'm okay.

37:41.926 --> 37:43.803
Let's go to a hospital just in case.

37:44.721 --> 37:46.097
I'm good.

37:47.599 --> 37:49.350
I'll give you my number, then.

37:49.434 --> 37:50.769
See a doctor, then call me.

37:52.103 --> 37:53.813
What a hassle.

38:06.409 --> 38:07.494
Here you go.

38:07.577 --> 38:08.912
Thank you.

38:09.412 --> 38:11.039
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

38:20.298 --> 38:21.633
KIM WOOJU

38:22.175 --> 38:23.551
"Kim Wooju"?

38:36.731 --> 38:39.317
Yes, that's my name.

38:47.367 --> 38:48.701
You piece of dirt.

38:50.370 --> 38:52.163
Why did you ignore my calls?

38:52.872 --> 38:54.165
Me?

38:54.415 --> 38:55.542
You punk!

38:55.625 --> 38:57.919
Do you think avoiding me will work?

38:59.045 --> 39:01.172
Why would I avoid you? I'm not like that.

39:06.719 --> 39:07.720
You're not?

39:09.556 --> 39:10.723
Take responsibility, then.

39:10.807 --> 39:12.100
"Take responsibility?"

39:12.183 --> 39:13.184
Aah!

39:14.185 --> 39:15.311
You want a settlement?

39:15.395 --> 39:17.814
Whatever. Hand it over right now.

39:17.897 --> 39:18.982
Fine.

39:19.065 --> 39:20.608
How much do you want?

39:21.609 --> 39:22.610
A hundred million won.

39:23.486 --> 39:25.989
- A hundred million won?
- Yes, that's right.

39:26.322 --> 39:28.408
What is wrong with you?

39:28.491 --> 39:29.742
Do you take me for a pushover?

39:29.826 --> 39:31.369
You're being unreasonable.

39:31.828 --> 39:33.121
You're the unreasonable one.

39:33.204 --> 39:34.372
Do as I say.

39:34.455 --> 39:35.582
- Hand it over.
- What?

39:35.665 --> 39:37.208
It's my mom's money.

39:37.292 --> 39:39.460
Hand it over, punk.

39:39.544 --> 39:40.545
You're insane.

39:44.257 --> 39:47.093
Why are you asking me
for the money to give to your mom?

39:49.679 --> 39:51.014
Where do you think you're going?

39:54.100 --> 39:55.143
Where are you going?

39:56.686 --> 39:58.271
What do you think you're doing?

39:59.147 --> 40:00.940
Get out of my car.

40:01.399 --> 40:02.525
I won't.

40:07.697 --> 40:08.948
What the...

40:10.033 --> 40:11.534
Drive on.

40:11.618 --> 40:12.785
My goodness.

40:21.169 --> 40:23.212
Why are you so strong?

40:24.589 --> 40:25.673
- Get out.
- No.

40:27.717 --> 40:28.843
Get out.

40:31.638 --> 40:32.931
Come here.

40:33.681 --> 40:35.808
- Will you stop it?
- Get out already.

40:35.892 --> 40:37.185
Leave me alone.

40:37.268 --> 40:38.519
Stop it.

40:39.395 --> 40:40.480
Darn you.

40:50.406 --> 40:53.326
If you don't stop this,
I'll call the police.

40:56.913 --> 40:58.039
Hey, you.

41:05.254 --> 41:07.173
What are you doing now?

41:07.256 --> 41:08.424
You can't go.

41:09.384 --> 41:11.844
Why do you keep trying to get away?

41:15.139 --> 41:16.933
- Is she crazy?
- Shouldn't we stop her?

41:17.016 --> 41:18.101
You want to run away?

41:18.184 --> 41:19.602
Hey, are you seeing this?

41:19.686 --> 41:20.687
Should we do something?

41:20.770 --> 41:22.063
- What's wrong with her?
- I don't know.

41:35.994 --> 41:37.161
Hey.

41:38.579 --> 41:41.040
Aren't you being too hard on me?

41:43.751 --> 41:46.671
You cheated on me.

41:47.463 --> 41:50.341
What makes you think you're in the right?

41:50.425 --> 41:54.012
- What?
- Why are you doing this to me?

41:54.679 --> 41:57.974
Why are you making me do this?

41:59.684 --> 42:01.811
I became a divorcée

42:02.812 --> 42:04.355
without ever getting
to walk down the aisle.

42:05.982 --> 42:07.692
My mom...

42:07.775 --> 42:10.278
It will break her poor heart.

42:11.529 --> 42:13.990
What about my mom?

42:14.407 --> 42:18.703
I can't tell her the truth.

42:22.832 --> 42:25.168
Mom...

42:26.878 --> 42:31.090
Mom, what should I do?

42:31.883 --> 42:33.885
Mom...

42:34.927 --> 42:36.345
Hey, are you all right?

42:37.764 --> 42:38.765
You...

42:39.432 --> 42:40.933
I don't think you are.

42:43.519 --> 42:44.562
You're...

43:04.957 --> 43:07.502
- It hurts!
- You...

43:10.505 --> 43:11.506
Come here.

43:12.548 --> 43:14.884
Help me.

43:14.967 --> 43:16.344
Why would you...

43:33.694 --> 43:35.363
How many did we get?

43:35.446 --> 43:37.073
A total of 17.

43:37.156 --> 43:38.407
Did we get everything?

43:38.491 --> 43:39.700
There's one more over there.

43:39.784 --> 43:41.077
Oh, here it is.

43:50.378 --> 43:52.338
We're done.

43:53.339 --> 43:55.299
Don't shower for the next two days.

43:55.383 --> 43:57.426
I'll prescribe you
a painkiller and antibiotics.

43:57.510 --> 43:59.053
Okay.

44:01.472 --> 44:03.141
Hey, how did it happen?

44:03.224 --> 44:04.642
Wasn't she drunk?

44:04.725 --> 44:07.061
She reeked of alcohol.

44:07.520 --> 44:09.522
How could you confuse

44:09.605 --> 44:11.315
a cactus for a stool
because you were drunk?

44:11.399 --> 44:14.193
Sitting on a cactus must be so painful.

44:39.760 --> 44:42.889
It'll throb for a few days,
but she'll be fine.

44:44.098 --> 44:46.559
It's usually a job for the interns,

44:46.642 --> 44:48.769
but I did it myself because you asked.

44:48.853 --> 44:51.147
Thanks, Jingyeong.

44:51.647 --> 44:54.192
- You were the first to come to mind.
- What?

44:54.275 --> 44:55.943
Only when you need help?

44:56.027 --> 44:58.237
You've been back for a month,
and you never called.

44:59.405 --> 45:00.531
How did you know I was back?

45:00.615 --> 45:03.576
My dad is your grandmother's doctor.

45:04.368 --> 45:05.953
He heard it during her checkup.

45:06.037 --> 45:07.246
Aah!

45:07.330 --> 45:08.623
So...

45:09.248 --> 45:11.417
Who is that woman?

45:11.500 --> 45:12.543
Your girlfriend?

45:12.627 --> 45:13.961
It didn't seem so.

45:14.045 --> 45:15.046
My girlfriend?

45:15.546 --> 45:17.006
As if she'd be my girlfriend.

45:17.798 --> 45:20.092
She's just some drunk I met in the street.

45:20.176 --> 45:21.469
She bumped into my car.

45:23.012 --> 45:25.348
You did that to her?

45:25.806 --> 45:27.683
What? Well, no.

45:28.684 --> 45:30.186
It's a long story.

45:30.269 --> 45:31.520
I'll tell you another time.

45:32.271 --> 45:35.149
Do you work late all the time?

45:35.816 --> 45:38.110
Yes, I'm preparing for a conference,

45:38.194 --> 45:40.112
so I have to stay up for a whole week.

45:43.449 --> 45:44.659
I'm so tired.

45:47.286 --> 45:49.413
Cover your mouth when you yawn.

45:55.211 --> 45:56.295
Wooju.

45:57.964 --> 46:00.258
I treated her, so you owe me a coffee.

46:00.341 --> 46:01.342
A coffee?

46:01.801 --> 46:02.843
Sounds good.

46:07.848 --> 46:09.850
What's wrong with her?

46:09.934 --> 46:11.435
I told her to get an X-ray.

46:13.980 --> 46:15.356
Hey, Jingyeong.

46:15.439 --> 46:16.774
The coffee has to wait.

46:17.400 --> 46:18.651
Wooju.

46:19.318 --> 46:20.861
Kim Wooju!

46:23.447 --> 46:25.366
Couldn't he even stay for a coffee?

46:37.461 --> 46:40.006
I could take a taxi.

46:41.716 --> 46:42.717
And sit like that?

46:46.804 --> 46:49.181
You must've been so flustered earlier.

46:49.265 --> 46:51.892
The alcohol must've made me lose my mind.

46:53.060 --> 46:55.646
I know you thought I was a weirdo.

46:57.189 --> 47:00.860
To be honest, I had a bad day today.

47:00.943 --> 47:04.030
I can't go into detail
since we just met, but...

47:05.239 --> 47:06.824
I mistook you for someone else.

47:06.907 --> 47:09.118
You happened to have the same name.

47:13.372 --> 47:17.835
By the way,
I don't need to get an arm X-ray.

47:19.128 --> 47:21.380
It was just a slight bump...

47:24.842 --> 47:28.012
I smell the alcohol whenever you talk.

47:28.971 --> 47:30.014
I feel dizzy.

47:44.820 --> 47:46.072
Excuse me.

47:46.155 --> 47:47.281
I'm really sorry,

47:47.823 --> 47:48.991
but could you pull over?

47:50.451 --> 47:51.452
What for?

47:51.535 --> 47:53.621
Going backwards gives me motion sickness.

47:53.704 --> 47:55.581
Seriously?

47:57.333 --> 47:58.626
Fine.

47:58.709 --> 47:59.710
Thank you.

48:30.866 --> 48:31.992
Are you all right?

48:56.058 --> 48:57.852
The sun is rising.

49:01.939 --> 49:04.442
It's like a red flower...

49:06.944 --> 49:09.238
blooming through the dark.

49:13.617 --> 49:16.078
Even though my world crumbles,

49:16.996 --> 49:18.456
the sun still rises,

49:19.540 --> 49:21.834
and morning still comes.

49:26.672 --> 49:29.341
There's always a way out, right?

49:33.304 --> 49:36.807
It feels as if Mother Nature...

49:38.767 --> 49:41.270
is giving me a message.

49:48.527 --> 49:50.321
The message must be "feed me."

49:56.368 --> 49:58.329
I'm the type...

50:00.498 --> 50:03.375
who must eat breakfast every morning.

50:04.877 --> 50:06.754
Would you like to get breakfast?

50:06.837 --> 50:08.005
It'll be my treat.

50:08.088 --> 50:10.049
I know a good hangover soup place nearby.

50:10.132 --> 50:11.467
No, thanks.

50:12.009 --> 50:13.010
Let's go.

50:13.093 --> 50:14.386
Okay.

50:49.922 --> 50:51.549
Thank you.

50:55.678 --> 50:57.304
About your arm.

50:58.597 --> 51:01.100
You should get it checked.

51:01.183 --> 51:02.351
Don't complain about it later.

51:02.851 --> 51:03.852
Okay.

51:04.311 --> 51:06.438
Thanks so much for everything today.

51:06.939 --> 51:09.567
Text me your account details.
I'll wire you the gas--

51:30.379 --> 51:32.590
What is wrong with me?

51:35.134 --> 51:36.468
Oh, whatever.

51:40.848 --> 51:42.391
It hurts.

51:50.524 --> 51:54.403
Where every step
and every breath carries elegance.

51:55.237 --> 51:57.031
Where life becomes art.

51:57.114 --> 51:58.699


51:59.325 --> 52:01.201
It's Beauté Palace.

52:02.578 --> 52:04.163
Beauté Department Store's
wedding festival

52:04.246 --> 52:06.248
is for newlyweds
who want a great beginning.

52:06.332 --> 52:08.834
A Beauté Palace unit
worth five million dollars

52:08.917 --> 52:11.170
you just saw in the video
is the grand prize.

52:11.253 --> 52:12.296
Yes, that's right.

52:12.379 --> 52:14.340
It's Beauté Construction's
ambitious new project,

52:14.423 --> 52:16.967
a high-end luxury town house.

52:17.051 --> 52:20.554
It gathered a lot of attention,
and so many entered the raffle.

52:20.638 --> 52:23.974
The couple that wins the apartment
must be so pleased.

52:24.058 --> 52:26.602
I'd have delayed my wedding
if only I'd known.

52:26.685 --> 52:28.646
I'm so sad I'm not a newlywed!

52:30.314 --> 52:32.358
- Shall we pick the winners?
Yes.

52:37.279 --> 52:39.740
Everyone wants one of these at home.

52:39.823 --> 52:42.534
A must-have
for the fashion-conscious, a styler!

52:43.494 --> 52:45.829
Why make a huge fuss when it's rigged?

52:46.747 --> 52:48.791
It must look real to avoid complaints.

52:50.000 --> 52:51.001
You think?

52:52.503 --> 52:54.088
I'm sure you took care of it.

52:54.171 --> 52:55.506
Congratulations.

52:55.589 --> 52:56.715
What do I do now?

52:57.383 --> 52:58.592
One, zero,

52:59.635 --> 53:01.679
seven, three!

53:01.762 --> 53:03.889
Ha Minyeong, congratulations!

53:03.972 --> 53:05.683
LEE SEONGGYU
DATE ENTERED: APRIL 12

53:05.766 --> 53:06.975
Lee Seonggyu.

53:07.726 --> 53:08.852
The mayor's wife's nephew?

53:08.936 --> 53:10.521
Yes, that's right.

53:25.911 --> 53:26.912
In case I get mixed up.

53:30.916 --> 53:34.211
Beauté Department Store's
30th anniversary wedding festival.

53:34.294 --> 53:38.257
It's time to select
the winner of the grand prize.

53:38.340 --> 53:41.218
Let's not waste time and get right to it.

53:41.301 --> 53:45.764
Beauté Department Store's CEO
will select the grand prize winner.

53:45.848 --> 53:47.224
Sir! Come on up.

54:27.681 --> 54:30.809
Our CEO is doing his best
to select the right winner.

54:33.187 --> 54:34.396
Give him some applause!

54:52.581 --> 54:53.832
He picked a ticket at last.

54:54.625 --> 54:57.169
The grand prize,
the Beauté Palace unit goes to...

54:57.628 --> 54:58.670
Please announce the winner.

55:00.297 --> 55:04.843
As the CEO of Beauté Department Store,
I will announce the winner myself.

55:05.761 --> 55:06.762
The grand prize winner is...

55:41.380 --> 55:42.589
Hello?

55:43.632 --> 55:44.675
Is this Ms. Yoo Meri?

55:44.758 --> 55:47.177
This is Beauté Department Store's PR Team.

55:50.180 --> 55:51.265
A raffle?

55:52.891 --> 55:55.143
What raffle do you mean?

55:55.227 --> 55:58.272
2 MONTHS AGO

55:59.898 --> 56:01.275
Sorry.

56:06.655 --> 56:07.781
WIN A TOWNHOUSE WORTH FIVE MILLION!

56:11.410 --> 56:12.452
YOO MERI
DATE ENTERED: APRIL 15

56:13.620 --> 56:16.623
If I win,
I'll spend the rest of my life...

56:17.457 --> 56:20.377
No, I'll do good even in the afterlife.

56:37.060 --> 56:38.478
Oh, that.

56:39.855 --> 56:41.398
I won?

56:42.524 --> 56:43.525
What?

56:44.401 --> 56:45.611
Yes.

56:45.694 --> 56:48.155
Yes, that's me. I'm Yoo Meri.

56:49.239 --> 56:51.074
Yes, of course. I'm sure it's me.

56:51.158 --> 56:53.160
Congratulations, Ms. Yoo.

56:53.243 --> 56:54.995
I need to confirm your identity.

56:55.078 --> 56:57.289
Can you send us a few documents?

56:58.123 --> 56:59.166
Oh, documents.

56:59.249 --> 57:00.834
Yes, of course, I'll send them.

57:00.917 --> 57:02.294
Give me a moment.

57:07.758 --> 57:08.967
Yes, I'm ready.

57:09.051 --> 57:10.469
A copy of your ID card.

57:10.552 --> 57:12.012
A copy of my ID.

57:12.929 --> 57:14.181
Proof that you don't own a home.

57:14.431 --> 57:16.933
Proof that I don't own a home.

57:18.101 --> 57:19.478
Proof of income,

57:19.561 --> 57:21.647
and proof of marriage. That's it.

57:21.730 --> 57:23.190
Proof of...

57:23.273 --> 57:25.233
- Proof of marriage?
- Yes.

57:25.317 --> 57:28.362
To be eligible to win, you must make
less than 80 million won a year

57:28.445 --> 57:30.489
and be newlyweds who don't own a home.

57:31.948 --> 57:34.326
Yes, okay. I understand.

57:34.826 --> 57:35.827
Bye.

57:40.916 --> 57:42.209
Proof of marriage?

57:44.419 --> 57:45.629
Will they cancel my win

57:46.630 --> 57:48.423
if I say I'm divorced?

57:53.303 --> 57:54.388
I didn't hand that thing in.

58:02.562 --> 58:03.814
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

58:06.650 --> 58:08.110
DIVORCE DECREE

58:08.193 --> 58:09.361
I still have it.

58:15.575 --> 58:17.703
Since I haven't handed it in yet...

58:18.078 --> 58:19.287
FAMILY REGISTRATION DETAILS

58:21.540 --> 58:22.791
SPOUSE: KIM WOOJU

58:26.211 --> 58:27.713
I'm still legally married.

58:31.633 --> 58:32.759
THIS DOCUMENT CERTIFIES THE ABOVE DETAILS

58:44.312 --> 58:46.398
I checked everything thoroughly.

58:47.065 --> 58:49.401
They're newlyweds
who got married five months ago,

58:49.484 --> 58:50.694
don't own a home,

58:50.777 --> 58:52.362
and their income meets the criteria, too.

58:52.446 --> 58:54.740
She meets every requirement completely.

58:57.451 --> 59:00.120
Shall we go ahead with the award ceremony?

59:00.996 --> 59:02.539
Our CEO should attend as well.

59:02.622 --> 59:03.749
- Postpone it for now.
- Okay.

59:04.708 --> 59:07.002
What? To when?

59:10.213 --> 59:13.467
Well, Yoo Meri said
her husband couldn't come.

59:13.550 --> 59:16.595
If we push back the ceremony,
I need to ask her if they'll be free.

59:17.512 --> 59:18.680
Her husband can't come?

59:20.432 --> 59:21.516
Why not?

59:21.600 --> 59:24.478
I talked to her on the phone earlier.

59:25.395 --> 59:27.105
Yes, I got all the documents.

59:28.273 --> 59:31.067
Will your husband be abroad for a while?

59:31.151 --> 59:32.360
Well...

59:33.695 --> 59:35.405
I don't see why you can't come alone.

59:35.489 --> 59:37.657
- That's a no.
- What?

59:37.741 --> 59:39.534
Didn't you read the fine print?

59:42.204 --> 59:44.080
The fine print?

59:44.164 --> 59:48.084
Yes, I just noticed the fine print
of the terms and conditions.

59:48.168 --> 59:49.294
"The win will be canceled

59:49.377 --> 59:52.088
if it turns out they lied
on any of the documents,

59:52.172 --> 59:55.467
and the winner will be held
legally responsible."

59:58.804 --> 01:00:00.055
And also...

01:00:01.515 --> 01:00:05.268
"The winner must actively participate in
any company promotions,

01:00:05.352 --> 01:00:08.605
and they must attend
the award ceremony as a couple."

01:00:08.688 --> 01:00:09.773
That's a must.

01:00:09.856 --> 01:00:11.233
There are no exceptions.

01:00:11.733 --> 01:00:12.776
What?

01:00:13.360 --> 01:00:16.279
You said earlier today
that it wouldn't matter.

01:00:16.363 --> 01:00:17.489
Why the sudden change?

01:00:18.740 --> 01:00:21.952
What happens if my husband can't make it?

01:00:25.247 --> 01:00:26.373
Then it will be canceled.

01:00:26.456 --> 01:00:29.125
It'll be canceled? That's not fair.

01:00:29.209 --> 01:00:31.294
I won the raffle. You just need me.

01:00:31.378 --> 01:00:33.213
Who cares if my husband's there or not?

01:00:33.296 --> 01:00:34.422
That's the rule.

01:00:35.131 --> 01:00:36.132
That's the rule.

01:00:36.216 --> 01:00:37.509
There's nothing I can do.

01:00:38.134 --> 01:00:39.219
Ah!

01:00:41.513 --> 01:00:43.431
CEO YOO MERI

01:00:44.140 --> 01:00:45.642
Okay, I got it for now.

01:00:45.725 --> 01:00:47.769
I'll be in touch.

01:00:52.774 --> 01:00:55.527
What kind of rule is that?

01:00:56.820 --> 01:00:57.988
This is madness.

01:01:07.539 --> 01:01:08.540
Give me a kiss.

01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:11.084
- I love you.
- I love you, too.

01:01:11.334 --> 01:01:13.086
MERI

01:01:16.548 --> 01:01:18.174
To leave a message,
press one.

01:01:18.258 --> 01:01:21.177
To leave your number, press two.

01:01:22.304 --> 01:01:23.638
Hello?

01:01:26.641 --> 01:01:29.227
It's me. I can't seem to reach you.

01:01:30.937 --> 01:01:33.899
I have something urgent to discuss.
Can you call me quickly?

01:01:35.650 --> 01:01:37.319
It's really important.

01:01:38.111 --> 01:01:41.364
I won a lucky draw kind of thing.

01:01:45.577 --> 01:01:46.912
This is paradise.

01:01:49.289 --> 01:01:50.290
Hey, baby.

01:01:51.291 --> 01:01:52.292
You're back.

01:01:53.752 --> 01:01:54.753
My cutie.

01:01:57.339 --> 01:01:58.381
Aren't you hungry?

01:01:58.465 --> 01:02:00.300
- Are you hungry, Jenny?
- Yes.

01:02:00.800 --> 01:02:02.427
- Shall we go eat?
- Yes.

01:02:03.970 --> 01:02:05.055
NEW MESSAGE

01:02:07.849 --> 01:02:08.934
YOU HAVE A NEW VOICE MESSAGE

01:02:09.017 --> 01:02:10.185
MERI

01:02:11.519 --> 01:02:12.729
Who is it from?

01:02:14.981 --> 01:02:15.982
It's a spam message.

01:02:19.653 --> 01:02:20.654
BLOCK CONTACT

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:21.863
BLOCK

01:02:23.281 --> 01:02:24.491
Let's go.

01:02:24.574 --> 01:02:25.742
Okay.

01:02:25.825 --> 01:02:28.620
WOOJU

01:02:31.206 --> 01:02:32.749
The call cannot be connected.

01:02:32.832 --> 01:02:34.834
Transferring to voicemail.

01:02:37.045 --> 01:02:40.340
Come on. Pick up.

01:02:42.467 --> 01:02:46.680
I can't do anything
if I can't talk to you.

01:02:56.022 --> 01:02:57.565
It's as good as out of my reach.

01:02:58.900 --> 01:03:00.276
It's a pie in the sky.

01:03:10.412 --> 01:03:11.579
This is Kim Wooju.

01:03:12.205 --> 01:03:14.249
I was wondering if you went to the doctor.

01:03:14.332 --> 01:03:16.960
No, I was too busy to...

01:03:19.462 --> 01:03:21.589
NO, I WAS TOO BUSY TO

01:03:23.133 --> 01:03:25.301
KIM WOOJU

01:03:38.690 --> 01:03:42.527
WHERE LIFE BECOMES ART

01:03:47.824 --> 01:03:49.743
KIM WOOJU

01:03:54.622 --> 01:03:55.957
KIM WOOJU

01:03:56.041 --> 01:03:57.375
He has the same name.

01:03:58.543 --> 01:04:01.629
The department store people
won't know if I bring someone else.

01:04:02.672 --> 01:04:04.007
They've never seen him.

01:04:25.403 --> 01:04:26.488
What did the doctor say?

01:04:26.946 --> 01:04:28.031
Did you get a doctor's note?

01:04:28.907 --> 01:04:30.116
Oh, the doctor.

01:04:32.160 --> 01:04:34.037
I was too busy to see one.

01:04:42.337 --> 01:04:43.713
Are you perhaps married?

01:04:45.340 --> 01:04:46.341
I'm sorry?

01:04:47.342 --> 01:04:50.220
Are you a married man?

01:04:51.179 --> 01:04:52.180
No, why?

01:04:52.639 --> 01:04:54.808
That's a relief.

01:04:54.891 --> 01:04:55.892
What is?

01:04:56.851 --> 01:04:59.479
I gave it a lot of thought.

01:05:00.105 --> 01:05:04.484
I know it's rash to say this
when we've only met once,

01:05:05.193 --> 01:05:06.986
but you're the only one I can turn to.

01:05:10.782 --> 01:05:12.534
Could you...

01:05:14.410 --> 01:05:15.703
be my husband?

01:06:01.166 --> 01:06:03.835
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:06:03.918 --> 01:06:05.628
You'll pay me
to play your fake husband

01:06:05.712 --> 01:06:07.005
- for a day?
Yes.

01:06:07.088 --> 01:06:10.758
I'm not kind enough
to be generous to a scammer.

01:06:10.842 --> 01:06:12.051
The husband must be present.

01:06:12.135 --> 01:06:13.303
Otherwise, we'll redraw.

01:06:13.386 --> 01:06:15.180
- Are they in?
- They'll call after discussing.

01:06:15.263 --> 01:06:17.307
You quit as team leader if you fail.

01:06:17.390 --> 01:06:20.393
I lost everything in a rental con,
but I won a five-million-dollar house.

01:06:20.476 --> 01:06:22.854
- I just need a husband to tag along.
You won a prize?

01:06:22.937 --> 01:06:24.480
So, that's what this is all about.

01:06:24.564 --> 01:06:27.650
Do you have any idea
how risky this scam is?

01:06:27.734 --> 01:06:28.860
It's me. How have you been?

01:06:28.943 --> 01:06:30.069
I'm in Seoul.

01:06:30.153 --> 01:06:31.863
I'm one of the residents here.

01:06:31.946 --> 01:06:34.866
- Over there?
That one?

01:06:36.951 --> 01:06:38.953
Translated by Jennifer Jean Lim
